{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovTraceUnique"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.param_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.param_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L119-L124","doc":"**The Markov parameter is zero iff the trace vanishes on `σ₀`** — so a Markov trace is the\nsymmetrising trace exactly when `tr₁(σ₀) = 0`.  (Forward direction is `param_eq`; this records it\nin the form used to read `z = 0` off a trace.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.tr_cosetFam_eq_delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.tr_cosetFam_eq_delta","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L109-L117","doc":"**The symmetrising-trace form**: a `z = 0` Markov trace is `δ` on the coset basis — `1` at the\nidentity index and `0` at every other one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetFam_cosetOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetFam_cosetOne","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L101-L107","doc":"`cosetFam` at the identity index is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L94-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetOne","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L89-L92","doc":"The identity index (all `jₖ = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.tr_cosetFam_of_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.tr_cosetFam_of_zero","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L71-L87","doc":"**A Markov trace with `z = 0` is the symmetrising trace.**  On the coset basis it is `1` at the\nidentity (the unique index of length `0`) and `0` everywhere else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen_succ","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L68-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetLen","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SymmetrisingTraceZeroParam.lean#L60-L64","doc":"The **length** of a coset-family index: the total number of generators in\n`cosetFam m p = ι(⋯ι(r_{j₁})⋯) · r_{j_m}`, i.e. `Σ jₖ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}